---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Pricing"
	description="Simple monthly pricing for pottery studios of every size. Starter, Studio and Collective plans, all with a 30-day free trial."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
			<h1>Pricing that grows with your studio</h1>
			<p class="lede narrow">
				Every plan includes unlimited classes, online payments and text reminders. Prices in USD,
				billed monthly. Save two months when you pay yearly.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section">
		<div class="plans">
			<div class="plan">
				<h2>Starter</h2>
				<p class="price">$29<span>/month</span></p>
				<p class="muted">For a home studio or a shared garage setup.</p>
				<ul>
					<li>1 kiln</li>
					<li>Up to 150 members</li>
					<li>Class and drop-in booking</li>
					<li>Firing fees by cubic inch</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="plan featured">
				<h2>Studio</h2>
				<p class="price">$79<span>/month</span></p>
				<p class="muted">Our most popular plan for community studios.</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Up to 3 kilns</li>
					<li>Unlimited members</li>
					<li>Wheel and table reservations</li>
					<li>Class packs, waitlists and memberships</li>
					<li>Pickup texts when pieces come out of the kiln</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="plan">
				<h2>Collective</h2>
				<p class="price">$149<span>/month</span></p>
				<p class="muted">For studios with more than one location.</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Unlimited kilns</li>
					<li>Multiple locations, one member account</li>
					<li>Staff roles and shift notes</li>
					<li>Priority support from a real potter</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>

		<p class="muted small">
			Card payments are processed by Stripe at their standard rate. Kilnbook does not add a booking
			fee on top.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Questions studios ask</h2>
		<dl class="faq">
			<dt>How does the free trial work?</dt>
			<dd>
				You get 30 days on the Studio plan with no card. At the end you pick a plan or your account
				pauses. Nothing is deleted.
			</dd>
			<dt>Can I import my members from a spreadsheet?</dt>
			<dd>
				Yes. Upload a CSV with names, emails and remaining class credits, and we map the columns for
				you during setup.
			</dd>
			<dt>What happens if I add a fourth kiln?</dt>
			<dd>
				You can move from Studio to Collective at any point in the month. We prorate the difference
				on your next invoice.
			</dd>
			<dt>Do you offer nonprofit pricing?</dt>
			<dd>
				Registered nonprofits and school ceramics programs get 30% off any plan. Mention it when you
				book a demo.
			</dd>
			<dt>Who owns my data if I cancel?</dt>
			<dd>
				Your data is yours. If you cancel, you can export your full member list, class history, and
				firing records as a CSV at any time before your account closes. We hold nothing back and keep
				nothing after you leave.
			</dd>
			<dt>What happens to my account when I cancel?</dt>
			<dd>
				Your account pauses rather than deletes. Members lose access to the booking portal, but
				everything — member records, kiln logs, class history — stays intact for 60 days so you can
				export or reactivate without starting over.
			</dd>
			<dt>Does Kilnbook work if we only run classes and don't do open studio?</dt>
			<dd>
				Yes. You can turn kiln queues and wheel reservations off entirely and use Kilnbook purely for
				class booking, class packs, and waitlists. It works the same way whether you run one class
				format or all three.
			</dd>
			<dt>We're a membership studio with no classes — is that a fit?</dt>
			<dd>
				Absolutely. Membership tiers, wheel-time reservations, firing queues, and the member portal
				all run independently of the class system. Many of our studios are open-access only.
			</dd>
			<dt>How do firing fees actually work?</dt>
			<dd>
				When a member submits a piece, they record its measurements. Kilnbook calculates the
				cubic-inch volume, applies your studio's rate, and charges the fee automatically when the
				piece is loaded. No spreadsheet, no mental math at the front desk.
			</dd>
			<dt>Do my members need to download an app?</dt>
			<dd>
				No. The member portal runs in any mobile browser — members can check their firing queue, book
				wheel time, and manage class packs without installing anything. There is no app to download.
			</dd>
			<dt>How does Kilnbook connect to Stripe?</dt>
			<dd>
				You connect your own Stripe account during setup. Payments go directly to your Stripe account;
				Kilnbook never holds your money. Kilnbook does not add a booking fee on top of Stripe's
				standard rate.
			</dd>
			<dt>Can members pay in person or do they have to pay online?</dt>
			<dd>
				Both. You can record cash and card-reader payments manually against any booking or
				membership. Online payments through Stripe are the default, but nothing forces members to pay
				that way.
			</dd>
			<dt>How long does onboarding take?</dt>
			<dd>
				Most studios are live within a week. Setup walks you through importing members, configuring
				your kiln slots and membership tiers, and setting your firing rates. We do a live walkthrough
				with every new studio on the Studio and Collective plans.
			</dd>
			<dt>What does support look like after we launch?</dt>
			<dd>
				Every plan has email support. Studio and Collective plans get a direct line to a team member
				who actually uses pottery studio software — not a support bot. Collective plans include
				priority response from a working potter on our team.
			</dd>
		</dl>
		<p>
			Still deciding? Read the <a href="/help/billing">billing FAQ</a> or
			<a href="/contact">talk to us</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</Base>
